<title>RUSSIA: Russian 1997 natural gas output to rise to 614 bcm.</title>
<headline>Russian 1997 natural gas output to rise to 614 bcm.</headline>
<dateline>MOSCOW 1997-04-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Russian natural gas output in 1997 will rise to 614 billion cubic metres (bcm), from 601 bcm in 1996, Fuel and Energy Minister Pyotr Rodionov told an energy conference on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The State Statistics Committee has put Russia's total gas output in 1996 at 575 bcm. Gas monopoly RAO Gazprom accounts for around 95 percent of Russia's total gas output.</p>
<p>Rodionov submitted his resignation last week.</p>
<p>--Mike Collett-White, Moscow Newsroom, +7095 941 8520</p>
</text>
